; An exchange ratio written where a rate goes.
;
; A takeover paying half a share of the acquirer for each share held, plus a
; little cash for the fraction left over. `@ 0.5 NASDAQ.NEWCO` is the ratio,
; not what the holding is worth, and a split's value is in the transaction's
; currency — CAD here, off the cash posting — so there is no reading of 0.5 that
; answers the question this tool has to ask.
;
; Applied as a rate regardless, the 100 shares given up were valued at
; 100 × 0.5 = 50.00 CAD, a figure with no source in the file.
;
; What this fixture produces: a refusal naming the posting, the commodity its
; rate is in, and the currency the entry is denominated in.
;
; Verified by tests/integration/test_beancount_reads_what_a_person_writes.py.
2024-01-01 commodity CAD
    gnucash-mnemonic: "CAD"
    gnucash-namespace: "CURRENCY"
    gnucash-fullname: "Canadian Dollar"
    gnucash-fraction: "100"
2024-01-01 commodity NASDAQ.OLDCO
    gnucash-mnemonic: "OLDCO"
    gnucash-namespace: "NASDAQ"
    gnucash-fullname: "Old Company Inc"
    gnucash-fraction: "1"
2024-01-01 commodity NASDAQ.NEWCO
    gnucash-mnemonic: "NEWCO"
    gnucash-namespace: "NASDAQ"
    gnucash-fullname: "New Company Inc"
    gnucash-fraction: "1"
